    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0206" n="126" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/1343</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Shidehara</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Castle</hi>)<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d108-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-24">May 24, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 66/T1</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    receipt of your Note dated May 21, 1930,<anchor n="29" xml:id="d108-f2"/>
                    relative to the interpretation of the term “category” <pb facs="0207" n="127"
                        xml:id="pg127"/> appearing in Article 19 of the London Naval Treaty of
                    1930.</p>
                <p>The Imperial Government understands the word “category” appearing in Article 19
                    of the above-mentioned treaty to mean “category” or “sub-category;” thus, it
                    interprets this treaty in the sense that ships belonging to either sub-category
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) or sub-category (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>) of the cruiser category (Article 16) which shall become over age
                    may be replaced only within that sub-category.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Baron Kijuro
                        Shidehara</hi></signed><lb/>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
